#!/usr/bin/python3
# A domain user's Group Policy at sign-in (D1): drive maps, logon scripts and
# user registry policy.
#
#   sg-gpo-user USER UID DIR
#
# Run as root by sg-domain-logon. The list of GPOs that apply to the user --
# their OU chain, link order, enforced links, security filtering on their
# token -- is Samba's (samba.gp.gpclass.get_gpo_list, the machine account's
# credentials), and so is the download of those GPOs from SYSVOL. What is
# done with them is ours, as Windows' client-side extensions would:
#
#   User\Preferences\Drives\Drives.xml   Group Policy Preferences drive maps
#                                        (MS-GPPREF): mapped with the user's
#                                        own ticket by sg-netmountd
#   User\Scripts\scripts.ini [Logon]     logon scripts: appended to
#                                        DIR/logon-script, run by the session
#   User\Registry.pol                    the user's registry policy: converted
#                                        to DIR/user-policy.reg, imported into
#                                        HKCU by the session
#
# Everything is best effort: a sign-in never fails because Group Policy did.
#
